WEBVTT

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:13.860
What's the current situation?

00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:16.690
We're tracking three Savages.

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:19.370
There's damage to the Zwei Island city block.

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:22.150
Evacuation of citizens is nearly complete.

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:25.840
Hayato-sama! Emile-sama!

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:27.960
Mei-Mai? What are you doing here?

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.750
I'm working.

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:33.280
Chris-sama, you should take your post, too.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:34.460
Roger that.

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:39.760
Chris-sama is the main analyst here.

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:41.540
Main analyst?

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:42.990
But isn't he in middle school?

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:46.270
Forget your average middle or high schooler,

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:52.160
his brains and skills put him above even
Warslarn HQ's intelligence division.

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:53.480
He truly belongs here.

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:55.230
Wow.

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:57.030
I'm honored.

00:00:57.410 --> 00:01:00.170
We have visual on the third Savage.

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:01.290
Putting it on the main screen.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:04.290
It's huge.

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:06.670
A giant.

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:08.700
It's a Trenta-class.

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:11.790
Its estimated ability values are unknown.

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:13.980
We have to deal with one of those...

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:16.200
Claire-sama, prepare to sortie.

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:20.550
On second thought, Charlotte Dimandius,

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:24.550
I'm going to pass on deploying Emile Crossfode
and Kisaragi Hayato today.

00:01:25.390 --> 00:01:27.170
They may have your recommendation,

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:29.600
but they have zero experience 
out in the field.

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:31.780
Dealing with a normal Savage
 would be one thing,

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:35.050
but a Trenta-class is too much
 for them to handle.

00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:36.570
So what's your plan?

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:39.640
Are the three of you going to
head out by yourselves?

00:01:41.230 --> 00:01:45.660
In a few hours, a Warslarn HQ 
support team will arrive,

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:47.500
so if we can just hold out until then...

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:48.890
Oh?

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:53.990
I never thought you would depend on
your older brother, CEO Judar Harvey.

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:56.840
My brother has nothing to do with this.

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:01.660
I'm just taking the best course of action
as captain of the <i>Little Garden.</i>

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:04.260
We're heading out, Liddy, Erica.

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:06.480
Right!

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:08.870
Wait, President.

00:02:08.870 --> 00:02:10.400
Please take us with you.

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:13.190
Did you not hear what I just said?

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:14.870
I did,

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:19.470
but weren't you the one who told us
about believing in "noblesse oblige"?

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.830
However, I believe in noblesse oblige!

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:28.040
Those with power should wield it 
for the sake of those without it.

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:31.640
A long time ago, 
I was attacked by the Savage

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:33.840
and lost part of my memories.

00:02:35.270 --> 00:02:37.510
If we wait for the support team to get there,

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:40.510
the city will just get destroyed.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:44.010
And so will the lives and
 memories of its residents.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:47.330
I'm not sure what I can do out there,

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:50.640
but I want you to let me go.

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:53.070
Just so you know,

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:56.310
I'm not the one who recommended
that these two go.

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:57.370
It was LiZA.

00:02:58.230 --> 00:02:59.070
LiZA did?

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:05.330
She said the best way to reduce casualties and
raise this operation's chances of success

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:11.040
was for Kisaragi Hayato and Emile Crossfode
to sortie along with you three.

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:13.040
Exactly.

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:16.130
Please let us, President.

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:18.550
Please!

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:23.110
I understand.

00:03:23.110 --> 00:03:25.800
If that's what LiZA has determined, 
I'll have to go along with it.

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:06.240
<b>Variant Awakening</b>

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:03.530
Okay, I'll be going over the operation.

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:05.850
First, Claire-sama, Liddy,

00:05:05.850 --> 00:05:09.050
and I will engage the standard 
Savage at point alpha.

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:10.490
Once we take it out,

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:13.540
we will engage the Trenta-class 
at point gamma.

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:18.020
Kisaragi Hayato and Emile Crossfode
are to move out then.

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:20.950
Please engage the standard 
Savage at point beta.

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:23.420
Why don't we all sortie together?

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:26.360
You two have zero experience 
out on the field.

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:30.840
We will go out ahead of you and 
show you how to fight the Savage.

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:34.020
In any event, once you take out 
the Savage at point beta,

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:35.910
your job is done.

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:38.710
We don't need to support you 
with the Trenta-class?

00:05:38.710 --> 00:05:41.320
Yeah, it looked really strong.

00:05:41.630 --> 00:05:42.680
Don't think so lowly of us!

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:46.600
How many Savages do you think 
we've eliminated up until this point?

00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:52.120
We've also encountered unknowns several times
and have taken them out each time.

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:54.700
Leave the Trenta-class to us.

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:12.120
First we take out the Savage's vision.

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:22.730
Liddy, Erica, let's go!

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:23.860
Right!

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:26.360
Hundred On!

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:34.450
That Hundred...

00:06:34.860 --> 00:06:36.760
It's an Arsène type

00:06:36.760 --> 00:06:40.480
which creates energy chains that can be
extended or retracted at will.

00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:42.860
Its name is Everlasting.

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:45.670
Now, Claire-sama!

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:54.300
Claire is aiming for the Savage's head.

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:56.310
In other words, its core.

00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:57.570
Take this!

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:02.710
A Savage's skin is said to be 
as strong as steel,

00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:06.400
but an attack from a Hundred 
can slice through it like butter.

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:07.940
That's the core!

00:07:08.410 --> 00:07:10.300
How about I finish you off?

00:07:13.710 --> 00:07:17.700
I have to teach those newcomers
 not to look down on us!

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:25.000
Pierce through!

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:29.340
Did you see that, Emile Crossfode?!

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:38.610
It's your turn next.

00:07:38.980 --> 00:07:41.800
Once you land at the coordinates, 
head to beta point immediately—

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:44.010
<i>We can't wait for this thing to land!</i>

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:48.730
The president and the others jumped off, 
so we should follow suit.

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:50.610
Right, Hayato?

00:07:54.250 --> 00:07:57.120
Hey! You need to hurry up 
and deploy your Hundred.

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:58.850
Wh-What is wrong with you?!

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:01.460
Hundred On!

00:08:08.540 --> 00:08:11.700
Hayato, let's try to do 
the same thing they did.

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:12.130
Huh?

00:08:12.430 --> 00:08:14.640
I'll fire some shots to 
provide a smokescreen.

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:17.480
Take that chance to attack the core.

00:08:18.580 --> 00:08:19.520
Got it.

00:08:30.220 --> 00:08:30.990
<i>That's tough.</i>

00:08:40.600 --> 00:08:41.410
Hayato!

00:08:41.810 --> 00:08:42.880
I know!

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:48.730
<i>I can't get all the way to the core.</i>

00:08:57.020 --> 00:08:58.050
This is it.

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:08.610
We did it, Hayato!

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:09.320
Huh?

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:15.450
Yeah.

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:19.030
Liddy!

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:20.700
Leave it to me.

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:37.720
Liddy! Erica!

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:47.890
Let's go save them, Emile!

00:09:47.890 --> 00:09:48.730
Yeah.

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:50.340
<i>There's no need for that.</i>

00:09:51.250 --> 00:09:53.580
You two stand by there.

00:09:53.970 --> 00:09:57.540
I told you the student council 
would take care of this one.

00:09:57.540 --> 00:09:58.320
<i>But...!</i>

00:09:58.660 --> 00:10:00.040
Silence!

00:10:10.760 --> 00:10:13.370
I'll destroy you along with the shelter.

00:10:16.250 --> 00:10:18.930
I'll destroy you along with the shelter.

00:10:29.870 --> 00:10:31.110
One more time...

00:10:32.910 --> 00:10:34.240
<i>There's not enough energy?</i>

00:10:34.990 --> 00:10:37.950
<i>Is that duel with Kisaragi Hayato 
still affecting me?</i>

00:10:41.290 --> 00:10:42.120
Claire-sama!

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:47.000
Claire-sama!

00:10:59.750 --> 00:11:01.210
Kisaragi Hayato?!

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:03.300
Are you okay?

00:11:05.320 --> 00:11:07.810
I told you to stand by...

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:11.510
There's no way I can just sit there and 
watch one of my own get done in.

00:11:13.460 --> 00:11:15.670
What's up with your hand?

00:11:15.670 --> 00:11:16.380
Huh?

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:20.070
Oh, I'm sorry!

00:11:20.800 --> 00:11:24.620
Why do you always steal my firsts?

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:27.190
I'm not really trying to...

00:11:27.190 --> 00:11:29.090
My first princess carry this time...

00:11:29.090 --> 00:11:30.500
That's what you're worried about?!

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:32.500
Claire-sama, you're about to get hit!

00:11:33.700 --> 00:11:34.620
This is bad!

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:36.770
Sorry, we'll have to dodge like this.

00:11:36.770 --> 00:11:37.420
<i>Wait!</i>

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:41.050
<i>What's going on, Erica?</i>

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:44.120
There's an airport in the direction 
the Savage is going to fire.

00:11:44.120 --> 00:11:47.560
If you dodge, the people there that are 
trying to evacuate will get hit.

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:49.740
President, what should I do?

00:11:49.740 --> 00:11:51.730
Put up a barrier and take the blast.

00:11:52.050 --> 00:11:53.820
You should be able to do it.

00:11:55.430 --> 00:11:57.070
Guess there's no time to hesitate.

00:12:02.140 --> 00:12:05.760
We're going to release our energy at 
the same time and blow the blast back.

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:06.410
Right.

00:12:07.630 --> 00:12:08.790
Let's go!

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:22.560
We did it, Kisaragi Hayato.

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:24.300
It's all thanks to you...

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:27.220
I-It's not like I did it for you.

00:12:27.890 --> 00:12:28.840
Oh.

00:12:29.320 --> 00:12:31.150
Are you not doing so well?

00:12:31.630 --> 00:12:35.450
Yeah, it's taking all my energy 
just to keep my armaments on.

00:12:35.450 --> 00:12:38.100
<i>That's quite the nice mood 
you two have going on there.</i>

00:12:38.100 --> 00:12:39.480
E-Emile?

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:42.950
I'm going to talk to you about this later.

00:12:56.350 --> 00:12:57.330
Emile!

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:25.230
Emilia!

00:13:37.240 --> 00:13:39.080
Are you okay, Emilia?

00:13:39.370 --> 00:13:40.370
Hayato?

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:43.930
Wait... Did you remember?

00:13:43.930 --> 00:13:45.090
Not all of it,

00:13:45.790 --> 00:13:49.300
but I know you're Emilia Hermit.

00:13:50.030 --> 00:13:51.480
Hayato...

00:13:51.480 --> 00:13:53.990
You saved me again.

00:13:54.740 --> 00:13:56.000
We'll talk later.

00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:57.880
Emilia, run now.

00:13:57.880 --> 00:13:58.360
But...!

00:13:58.360 --> 00:13:59.100
Hurry!

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:02.980
Take the vice president for me!

00:14:09.830 --> 00:14:11.250
Hayato!

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:31.010
Full-body armament...

00:14:32.480 --> 00:14:33.640
It's the same as before...

00:14:39.300 --> 00:14:40.250
Hayato....

00:14:43.720 --> 00:14:46.830
No, Hayato!
 You can't lose yourself!

00:15:13.390 --> 00:15:14.390
Vice President!

00:15:18.670 --> 00:15:20.530
Are you okay, Erica?

00:15:21.280 --> 00:15:22.400
Claire-sama...

00:15:23.230 --> 00:15:25.400
Th-Thank you.

00:15:26.630 --> 00:15:27.780
<i>Kisaragi Hayato,</i>

00:15:28.660 --> 00:15:30.610
<i>just what has gotten into you?</i>

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:37.610
You can't, Hayato!

00:15:39.180 --> 00:15:40.250
I guess there's no choice.

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:04.190
Emilia... I...

00:16:04.190 --> 00:16:05.270
I'll explain later.

00:16:05.950 --> 00:16:07.780
We need to finish him off.

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:12.250
Channel all your energy into your
Flying Swallow and destroy its core.

00:16:12.250 --> 00:16:13.660
Can I do it?

00:16:13.660 --> 00:16:16.280
You'll be fine now.

00:16:18.340 --> 00:16:19.290
Right.

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:23.530
Go!

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:54.580
I did it...

00:17:00.250 --> 00:17:01.700
You did it, Hayato.

00:17:02.810 --> 00:17:03.500
Yeah.

00:17:06.350 --> 00:17:08.360
Emile Crossfode...

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:16.050
Y-You've... got boobs...

00:17:16.500 --> 00:17:18.020
And in the middle of combat, you...

00:17:18.020 --> 00:17:21.020
You kissed Kisaragi Hayato...

00:17:22.440 --> 00:17:24.320
Guess you found me out.

00:17:42.020 --> 00:17:45.100
<i>We were able to protect all those people.</i>

00:17:45.580 --> 00:17:46.830
<i>And this place.</i>

00:17:47.650 --> 00:17:49.850
Isn't that great, Hayato?

00:17:49.850 --> 00:17:50.590
Yeah.

00:17:51.550 --> 00:17:57.720
We're able to go into combat
 because of moments like these.

00:18:02.270 --> 00:18:05.930
So you took out the Savage?

00:18:06.300 --> 00:18:08.080
It wasn't just me.

00:18:08.380 --> 00:18:11.330
The president, Emile,
 and everyone else helped.

00:18:11.830 --> 00:18:16.290
Anyway, it's unfortunate that
Sakura-san's concert got canceled.

00:18:15.610 --> 00:18:18.740
<b>The Savage Appeared on the Zwei Islands,
 Resulting In Damage</b>

00:18:16.290 --> 00:18:18.740
But I'm glad no one got hurt.

00:18:19.620 --> 00:18:22.890
Now you have to make up for worrying me.

00:18:23.370 --> 00:18:24.900
Silly.

00:18:30.590 --> 00:18:36.050
They told me I can keep pretending to be a guy
since it would get everyone up in arms otherwise.

00:18:36.050 --> 00:18:38.590
The president reluctantly agreed.

00:18:39.460 --> 00:18:40.360
But...

00:18:40.890 --> 00:18:43.470
...I can't stay in this room anymore.

00:18:44.060 --> 00:18:45.140
I see.

00:18:46.760 --> 00:18:48.890
Emile, I want you to tell me

00:18:49.500 --> 00:18:51.010
everything you know.

00:18:52.960 --> 00:18:55.900
First, I have to talk about Variants.

00:18:57.480 --> 00:18:58.650
Variants?

00:19:00.350 --> 00:19:03.450
So basically, because you 
were attacked by a Savage,

00:19:03.450 --> 00:19:06.540
you got infected with the Savage virus?

00:19:06.790 --> 00:19:07.560
That's right.

00:19:08.380 --> 00:19:12.220
And since you tried to suck out 
my blood to save me, you are as well.

00:19:14.110 --> 00:19:16.120
The virus is potent.

00:19:16.120 --> 00:19:18.160
Most people die from it.

00:19:18.740 --> 00:19:20.880
However, if you're lucky 
and you live through it,

00:19:20.880 --> 00:19:24.050
your Hundred score goes up incredibly,

00:19:24.050 --> 00:19:25.890
and you become extremely compatible.

00:19:26.550 --> 00:19:30.990
People like Char call
the infected people Variants.

00:19:31.750 --> 00:19:34.480
There aren't even ten of us
 in the entire world.

00:19:34.480 --> 00:19:37.720
So I knew I'd be able to see you again.

00:19:37.720 --> 00:19:42.660
I had Char checking the Hundred tests 
throughout the world.

00:19:42.660 --> 00:19:47.200
So that's why you knew I'd be coming here,
and came to the <i>Little Garden</i> yourself.

00:19:47.500 --> 00:19:52.890
I didn't think I'd be coming to the Warslarn school
that Char was assigned to, though.

00:19:52.890 --> 00:19:56.110
But why did you have to pretend to be a guy?

00:19:57.760 --> 00:19:58.830
Well...

00:19:59.550 --> 00:20:02.470
...I wanted to be in the same room as you.

00:20:04.360 --> 00:20:07.120
That's not the only reason, though.

00:20:07.120 --> 00:20:09.750
It'd be bad if people found out.

00:20:09.750 --> 00:20:12.190
Well, you can tell me about that later.

00:20:13.330 --> 00:20:17.070
So, the reason I lose my memories 
in the middle of a battle

00:20:17.070 --> 00:20:18.690
is because I'm a Variant?

00:20:19.120 --> 00:20:22.010
Yeah. When you're in danger of dying,

00:20:22.010 --> 00:20:25.390
the virus activates, you lose yourself, 
and go on a rampage.

00:20:26.050 --> 00:20:28.240
It's one of the characteristics 
of being a Variant.

00:20:28.730 --> 00:20:30.100
Then you too, Emile...

00:20:31.260 --> 00:20:34.180
But I've learned to control it with training.

00:20:34.690 --> 00:20:36.560
I wonder if I'll be able to do it, too.

00:20:36.560 --> 00:20:37.640
It'll be fine.

00:20:37.640 --> 00:20:39.810
You'll be able to control it 
if you undergo training.

00:20:39.810 --> 00:20:41.350
Let's do our best together.

00:20:41.350 --> 00:20:43.510
Yeah. Thanks.

00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:45.940
Hey, Hayato...

00:20:45.940 --> 00:20:46.780
Hm?

00:20:46.780 --> 00:20:50.140
That day in Gudenburg, and today...

00:20:50.530 --> 00:20:53.100
I want to thank you for saving me.

00:20:53.610 --> 00:20:56.360
I've always wanted to thank you.

00:20:58.190 --> 00:21:00.580
Oh, yeah. 
I need to make some tea.

00:21:00.580 --> 00:21:01.860
I'll do it.

00:21:07.390 --> 00:21:08.850
H-Hayato...

00:21:08.850 --> 00:21:12.070
If you give me a little more time, 
I wouldn't mind...

00:21:12.070 --> 00:21:13.620
Th-That's not it.

00:21:14.150 --> 00:21:15.210
My body just...

00:21:16.610 --> 00:21:19.800
Wait. Could this be a side effect 
of the virus activating?

00:21:28.990 --> 00:21:30.280
H-Hey.

00:21:30.280 --> 00:21:32.660
In order to suppress an activated virus,

00:21:32.660 --> 00:21:35.510
you need to administer an inactive virus.

00:21:36.060 --> 00:21:38.690
In other words, I just administered mine.

00:21:40.660 --> 00:21:43.220
Do you...

00:21:44.110 --> 00:21:46.280
...not like kissing me?

00:21:46.280 --> 00:21:49.200
N-No, that's not it,

00:21:49.200 --> 00:21:50.470
but...

00:22:00.220 --> 00:22:01.940
Emile Crossfode!

00:22:01.940 --> 00:22:04.350
I told you to move rooms immediately!

00:22:05.930 --> 00:22:08.130
P-President?!

00:22:08.830 --> 00:22:12.270
Wh-Wh-What are you two doing?!

00:22:12.270 --> 00:22:14.830
A-And you're on top of each other...

00:22:14.830 --> 00:22:17.020
No, we were just...!

00:22:25.490 --> 00:22:28.170
H-Hey, what are you doing?!

00:22:29.050 --> 00:22:30.700
I-I'm sorry!

00:22:30.700 --> 00:22:33.760
You took another one of my "firsts"...

00:22:33.760 --> 00:22:35.870
Th-That was an accident! An accident!

00:22:36.960 --> 00:22:38.620
I know that.

00:22:39.020 --> 00:22:41.200
You don't have to apologize.

00:22:42.390 --> 00:22:46.060
You know, you're being 
strangely nice to Hayato.

00:22:46.060 --> 00:22:48.190
You've been kind of weird since yesterday.

00:22:48.190 --> 00:22:50.470
Th-That's totally not true.

00:22:50.760 --> 00:22:52.610
Then why did you come here?!

00:22:52.610 --> 00:22:55.880
I wanted to make sure you left the room.

00:22:55.880 --> 00:22:57.620
It's my job, as student council president.

00:22:57.620 --> 00:23:01.030
If something bad happened, you know...

00:23:01.030 --> 00:23:02.690
Something bad?

00:23:02.690 --> 00:23:05.570
You kissed Hayato yourself!

00:23:05.820 --> 00:23:08.620
Hayato, kiss me again!

00:23:08.620 --> 00:23:11.000
I can't lose to the president!

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:14.200
Stop it, Emile Crossfode!

00:23:14.200 --> 00:23:15.870
Kisaragi Hayato, you too!

00:23:16.650 --> 00:23:20.650
And why do you have a problem 
with Hayato and me kissing?

00:23:32.880 --> 00:23:35.500
Too bad about the concert.

00:23:35.500 --> 00:23:36.450
Yeah...

00:23:37.000 --> 00:23:39.280
It's good no one was hurt, though.

00:23:40.080 --> 00:23:41.780
We'll have another chance.

00:23:42.100 --> 00:23:44.850
You can come to delight people
with your song then.

00:23:44.850 --> 00:23:45.480
Yeah.

00:23:47.110 --> 00:23:50.860
A video of the hero Slayer 
that saved the Zwei Islands...

00:23:52.120 --> 00:23:53.340
Hero...

00:24:00.790 --> 00:24:05.740
<b>Bodyguard</b>
